{"id": "EUVD-2026-103768", "enisaUuid": "f2d031fa-5c77-3354-ac10-e9f339a0da93", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: ath9k: reject short WMI command responses\n\nath9k_wmi_rsp_callback() removes the validated WMI header and copies\nthe number of bytes expected by the waiting command into its response\nbuffer. A device response shorter than that expectation can therefore\nbe read beyond the skb payload.\n\nRecord -EMSGSIZE for a short response, complete the waiter, and return\nthe stored status from the command path. This also prevents callers from\nconsuming stale response bytes as a successful reply.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:49:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:26:20", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/03ef61d05aa26022327f971b790f07e6bf6e35d6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e0c21130c1c7791ba73b19a3a9ea767c8cd43745", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a3b0137c855a61371d9cf9993b8bcc33c9798202", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/93ce8ea70451e800601bc9444aa33043de15d67b"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98828", "GHSA-hwh7-fwf3-88qj"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "14a84f6c-a875-33af-a036-341fe6f388ab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "16fb83a2-131a-3ccd-bb8b-6e39b30623bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "2c61bbab-f5bd-34a8-91d5-7249d0ca0e06", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fb9987d0f748c983bb795a86f47522313f701a08 <03ef61d05aa26022327f971b790f07e6bf6e35d6"}, {"id": "5a0be5c5-bc98-385c-8e0d-4a0b551f71e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "77db7c58-f2cd-32c5-b609-6a032d55066b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fb9987d0f748c983bb795a86f47522313f701a08 <a3b0137c8